course: dictionary
lesson: 11710
title: Augmentation: making bigger by adding
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Augmentation is a formal word. It means making something bigger, larger or stronger by adding to it. Its root is the word augment, which means to add to something. «The town made an augmentation to the library, adding a new reading room.» The town did not remove anything. It added a room, so the library got bigger.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Words like adding, extra, new and more tell you that something is growing. «The team needed an augmentation of players, so two more joined.» Two more players joined, so the team grew. Always ask: did something get added to make it bigger? If yes, augmentation fits.
explain: Augmentation can also name the thing that was added. «Her augmentation of the garden was a big new greenhouse.» Here the greenhouse is the augmentation. So the word can mean the action of adding, or the thing that has been added.
fact: Augmentation means making something bigger, larger or stronger by adding to it.
fact: Augmentation can also mean something that is added to make something larger.
fact: Augmentation is a formal word, so you will see it in serious writing and in school or work reports.
fact: In music, augmentation can mean making note lengths longer, so a note lasts for more beats.
fact: In medicine, augmentation can mean surgery that makes a body part bigger.
exercise: «The town made an augmentation to the library by adding a new reading room.» What does augmentation mean here? | A closed door | Lost books | *Something added to make the library bigger | A small mistake
exercise: Mia thinks augmentation means taking something away. What does it really mean? | Breaking something into pieces | Taking away a little bit at a time | Hiding something from view | *Making something bigger by adding to it
exercise: «The shop made an augmentation to its garden.» Which word is closest in meaning to augmentation? | silence | *extension | ruin | mistake
test: «The bridge had an augmentation: two new lanes were added so more cars could cross.» What is an augmentation? | *Something added to make it larger | A broken bridge | Something taken away to make it smaller | A type of paint
test: The plural of augmentation is | *augmentations | augmentationses | augmentation's | augmentate
exam: Which best matches the formal meaning of augmentation? | Losing something | *Making something bigger, larger or stronger by adding to it | Counting things | Making something quieter
